## Design Objectives
* This design is made to be 3D printed.
* The bottom chassis was designed to hold these hardware parts in place:
  - A 6v 150rpm dc motor with gear reduction for steering 
  - Two 6v 180rpm dc motor with gear reduction for drive
  - An ESP32
  - The outer surface body
  - A 9V battery
* A battery place lid is designed to make the battery exchange easier.
* Three motor holders are designed to hold the motors tightly in place. Holders use 4m screws.
* The wheels are designed to be wrapped up with rubber bands to increase the grip.
* A spur gear and a linear gear is designed for the steering mechanism of the car.

## Dimension Accuracy and Tolerances
* A tolerance of 0.3mm is applied to the rod holes.
* A tolerance of 0.2mm is applied to the linear-spur gear mechanism
* No tolerance is applied to the other parts as they require tightness


## Software Used
* Autodesk Fusion 360 is used at the design process of this project

